```c
/* For the before_stamp to be different than the write_stamp */
```
Reason:
The fix involves explicitly setting `before_stamp` to zero when an event is discarded. This ensures that `before_stamp` is always different from `write_stamp`, preventing any new event from using an invalid timestamp from the discarded event. This change guarantees that when a new event arrives, it will insert an absolute timestamp, thus maintaining correct timing information.

